# Build context exclusions — single source of truth for every stage
# (base / app / cicd / runtime). runtime derives FROM cicd derives FROM app, so
# there is no per-target difference worth keeping: the old .dockerignore.cicd
# was merged into this file and deleted.
#
# buildah picks this up automatically from the context root — do NOT pass
# --ignorefile unless you deliberately want a different filter.
#
# HARD CONSTRAINTS — paths the Dockerfile or the build scripts read; they must
# survive this filter:
#   backend/tests                        -> Dockerfile:358
#   backend/scripts/docker-entrypoint.sh -> Dockerfile:727
#   .build.env                           -> scripts/{install,npm_warmup}.sh
#
# Rules of thumb:
#   * Mirror .gitignore: what is not worth committing is not worth shipping.
#   * Hidden entries are FAIL-CLOSED. `**/.*` drops every hidden path at any
#     depth — directories AND files — because Docker's pattern matcher cannot
#     tell `.claude/` from `.env` by type, only by name. Leaving hidden files
#     in by default is how a nested `a/.env` leaks a password into the image.
#   * If a build ever needs a hidden file, un-exclude it explicitly below.
#     New hidden files do NOT enter the image until you do.

# --- Hidden entries at any depth: .git .github .claude .venv .pytest_cache
# --- frontend/.vite .buildah-storage-root ... ---
**/.*

# --- Whitelist: hidden files that must survive the rule above. Docker's
# --- pattern matcher cannot tell a hidden directory from a hidden file, so
# --- this list is how a hidden FILE opts back in. ORDER MATTERS: a `!` line
# --- only overrides exclusions that appear EARLIER in this file.
# ---
# --- .env is required at runtime — install.sh writes a systemd unit with
# --- EnvironmentFile=$DEST/.env — so the runtime image must contain it.
# --- NOTE: it carries HERMES_WEBUI_PASSWORD and TLS key paths and is baked
# --- into an image layer; rotate those if the image is ever shared.
!.env

# --- .build.env is read at BUILD time, from inside the image: scripts/npm_warmup.sh
# --- sources it (Dockerfile:517) and scripts/install.sh sources it during the
# --- --deps-only RUN (Dockerfile:581). Dropping it does NOT fail the build — it
# --- silently downgrades the warmup to its hardcoded playwright revisions and
# --- leaves the SDK install unpinned.
!.build.env

# --- Python cache / packaging junk (not hidden, so not caught above).
# --- `**/` prefix is required: unlike .gitignore, a bare `__pycache__/` in
# --- .dockerignore matches the root only and lets backend/__pycache__ through.
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd

# --- Node & frontend tooling (reinstalled inside the image). Same `**/`
# --- requirement as above — a nested node_modules must not slip through.
**/node_modules/
frontend/.tsbuildinfo

# --- Frontend build output. Every file here is regenerated during the image
# build: vite emits assets/ + index.html, copies frontend/public/ out as
# logo/ + observer.html, and `postbuild` copies @novnc/novnc into novnc/.
# Shipping a stale host copy is exactly why Dockerfile:608 has to `rm -rf`
# assets/ + index.html again. (Dockerfile's "repo-tracked" note about
# static/logo + observer.html is wrong — git tracks nothing under static/.)
frontend/dist/
static/

# --- Generated version badge — Dockerfile:240 overwrites it ---
backend/app/api/_version.py

# --- Not hidden, but never belong in an image ---
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
copilot-instructions.md
git_commit_head.txt

# --- Local-only review harness, scratch, backups ---
graphify-out/
archive/
*.bak
*.swp
*.swo

# --- Screenshots & transient artifacts ---
screenshot-*.png
full-UI.png

# --- Docs (the Dockerfile never reads them) ---
docs/

# --- Local buildah image store + runroot (BUILDAH_ROOT / BUILDAH_RUNROOT).
# Must never enter the build context: `COPY . /build` would walk the whole
# store, including live overlay `merged/` mountpoints (minutes of metadata
# I/O) and then bake it into the image. Also covered by **/.*; the explicit
# rules keep the "why" next to the names. The second pattern covers the
# misspelled runroot name currently used by the lab script.
.buildah-storage*/

# --- OS junk / logs ---
Thumbs.db
*.log

# --- Test artifacts only. The tests themselves are wanted (see HARD
# CONSTRAINTS above) — only their results are disposable.
backend/tests/.results/
frontend/tests/.results/
